In article <BOB.90Aug2151213@dolores.Stanford.EDU> bob@dolores.Stanford.EDU (Bob Lodenkamper) writes:
>    Closing your eyes?  Sensible, but I guess it makes things too
>easy.  What's the point of all those neat sounds if a player with
>only telepathy can always know what's on the level.

I've always thought that #close should give you the same display as a potion
of monster detection if you are telepathic. That means you can't use the '/'
key to find out what is what, but you get a rough idea of what is around. The
sounds tell you about fountains, sinks, etc, which are not apparent with
telepathy anyway; if you see a 'h' it might indeed be a dwarf but it could
also be a hobbit, '@' could be a shopkeeper or an elf, etc. Without the '/'
key you won't be able to find out.

